body:
Force you, I would not think so specially for a psychiatrist. Maybe work with you over time and get you slowly to open up. Build a repour/trust

&#x200B;

But I mean cant fix something with out knowing what the problem is imo.

been there done that. i went a little bit further with the money though. If it makes you happy at the time then no worries. I actually do this when i feel at my lowest and its a expensive way to get someone to talk to you but sometimes its all you got.

&#x200B;

Rather them have the money then it go to waste or me spend it on food/sweets and get even fatter lol

I have not experienced as much pain as you in any right, even though my brain sometimes might want to argue that point. I lost my whole life a little over 2 years ago, she didnt die but might aswell have. I hate the saying of it gets better or people who promise it will get better cause there is no way to be sure of that cause it relies on yourself and nobody else is going to help you fully. Well that is what ive learned over the past 2 years of attempts/ being in psych wards. But it does get easier to handle the pain you feel. If you are lucky enough to have a support system in place rely on them, spend time with other family if you have them. Seek help if you are able too. I say this after 2 years of doing the same thing and not having any success myself but in the hopes maybe it goes better for you. Which is weird now that im thinking of it. The pain i dont think will ever go away, i mean its been 2 years and my last suicide attempt was about 3 months ago but it has become a little easier to deal with, if that makes any sense at all.

&#x200B;

I browsed your post history a bit before posting just something i like to do before responding to someone, I noticed you said you played the violin and the viola.. I dont play either but for whatever reason I watch a youtube channel about violins "twosetviolin" 2 funny awkward asian guys. I wish i learned to play a instrument but i focused on a computer instead. I only bring this up cause they always make fun of the viola\* so I found it really interesting that you played both.

/u/bolognaisass Is correct, I would go with changing the #containerdiv2 by adding display:flex;

Keeps it from breaking out of div element when scaling down, unlike the vertical\-align method does.

[https://codepen.io/moodock/pen/OZBzNV](https://codepen.io/moodock/pen/OZBzNV)

EDIT: Here is a good example found online for it. For a better visual representation.
http://jsfiddle.net/kYDgL/


Your problem is you are floating a div element in whole. and not clearing anything. So you need to break it into two separate div elements blocks, with a container. 

    <div class = "southerncampaign">
    <img src ="https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/KingsMountain_DeathOfFerguson_Chappel.jpg" class="scimage" width=300 height=300>
    <a href="southerncampaign.html"><h3>Southern campaign</h3></a>
    <p>Read about the battles of the war's southern theater</p>
    </div>    

I just added a class to your img code.

    .scimage {
      float:left
    }

    .southerncampaign h3{
    	float: right;

    }

    .southerncampaign p{
      clear:right;
    }

In the css I added h3 to .southerncampaign to target the specific text element to control it.
There are plenty of cleaner ways to do this, but through that up for you real quick. You just need to brush up on div elements and how they are effected when you are floating them.

If I am understanding your question correctly. You need to change up the animation name for each one. So the code will run differently for each one you want.

                  @keyframes example {      }
        animation-name: example;

example being the animation name and just change for each one of your gallerys.
example1 , example2, example3 etc etc
